{"name":"Angel’s Sigh","hex":"#e2d9d3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incorporeal and holy or semidivine messenger from a deity or other divine entity, traditionally depicted as a youthful, winged figure in flowing robes.","A person having qualities traditionally attributed to angels."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To support by donating money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel"},{"term":"sigh","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale a larger quantity of air than usual, and immediately expel it; to make a deep single audible respiration, especially as the result or involuntary expression of fatigue, exhaustion, grief, sorrow, frustration, or the like.","To lament; to grieve."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, prolonged audible inhale and exhale of breath; as when fatigued, frustrated, grieved, or relieved; the act of sighing.","a manifestation of grief; a lament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sigh"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel","wikidata":"Q235113"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/500px-Angel_of_the